Python wrappers (adapted for JIT compilation):
- quant.py          — fused quantization helpers (per_warp_int8, per_channel_fp8, etc.)
- sm90_compile.py   — torch.library.custom_op wrappers for SM90 attention kernel
- core_sm90.py      — sageattn_qk_int8_pv_fp8_cuda_sm90 entry point

CUDA kernel sources (from csrc/):
- csrc/qattn/qk_int_sv_f8_cuda_sm90.cu  — SM90 attention kernel (WGMMA + TMA)
- csrc/qattn/attn_cuda_sm90.h
- csrc/qattn/pybind_sm90.cpp
- csrc/qattn/attn_utils.cuh
- csrc/fused/fused.cu       — fused quantization kernels
- csrc/fused/fused.h
- csrc/fused/pybind.cpp
- csrc/utils.cuh, math.cuh, wgmma.cuh, dispatch_utils.h,
  cp_async.cuh, numeric_conversion.cuh, permuted_smem.cuh, reduction_utils.cuh

- LICENSE (copied from upstream)

All files are retained with their original Apache-2.0 headers.
Python wrappers (quant.py, sm90_compile.py, core_sm90.py) have been modified
to use torch.utils.cpp_extension.load() for JIT CUDA compilation instead of
pre-compiled extension modules.
